<title>HUNGARY: Hungary's Dedasz reports 323 mln forints '96 loss.</title>
<headline>Hungary's Dedasz reports 323 mln forints '96 loss.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>					Jan-Dec 1996   As percentage</p>
<p>								 of</p>
<p>							   1995 figures</p>
<p>    Operating profit	     436.4		  n/a</p>
<p>    Pre-tax result		 323.7 loss	   n/a</p>
<p>    Net sales		   30,719.3		130.8</p>
<p>    Other revenue		  393.3		 85.4</p>
<p>    Direct cost of sales    27,902.7		120.6</p>
<p>    Indirect cost of sales   1,876.1		133.1</p>
<p>    Other expenditures	   897.4		109.7</p>
<p>    Net financial income	 753.4 loss	   n/a</p>
<p>	Financial revenue	   39.4		 25.0</p>
<p>	Financial expenditure    792.9		 91.2</p>
<p>NOTE - Dedasz is an electricity distribution company whichis traded on the Budapest over-the-counter market. Germany's Bayernwerk bought a 47.25 percent stake in it during privatisations in 1995.</p>
<p>The figures are unaudited.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom+36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
